          .num_remark{:id => "Pontrjagin duality"}
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+duality"}> Pontrjagin duality
                )
              %br/
              In the special case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma = S^1
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat G \,\coloneqq\, Hom(G,S^1)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+dual"} Pontrjagin dual
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %p
              In this case, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              so that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation action
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(G,S^1)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+action"} trivial
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiscreteQuotientSpace"} (2)
              is a special case of the classical fact that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+dual"} Pontrjagin dual
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+group"} compact topological group
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Pontrjagin+dual#BasicPropertiesOfDualGroups"} there
